body:
@QbieShay I respect your opinion, but my stance remains unchanged and opposed.

I think that when both trails and motion blur depend on the FPS, their effects tend to become much stronger when the frame rate drops. But, unlike trails which people often want the effect to be strong, the majority likely prefers motion blur to be as subtle as possible, so I believe normalization is needed to achieve stable (as subtle) results.

As for the maintainer poll, it is currently a flat 1-to-1 tie between you and me, so we will need the opinions of other maintainers.

